# Rust
target/
# Cargo.lock IS committed deliberately: core/Cargo.toml declares a real
# [[bin]] (pyreverseetl-dashboard), so this workspace produces an actual
# binary, not just a library - lockfiles for binary crates should be
# committed for reproducible builds (see https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/faq.html#why-do-binaries-have-cargolock-in-version-control).

